Spec: History map

Purpose:
  The map view of the History tab: every saved ride as a line coloured by activity type, an optional
    heatmap, and the preview of the tapped ride with its route's best time.

Owns:
  ./*.dart
  ./widgets/*.dart
  /test/history_map

References:
  /docs/decisions/0001-ride-outlines.md
  /lib/features/history/history.sdd
  /lib/map/map.sdd
  /lib/domain/ride_outline.sdd
  /lib/domain/outline_hit.sdd
  /lib/domain/heat_points.sdd
  /lib/domain/area_filter.sdd
  /lib/domain/route_group.sdd
  /lib/domain/activity_type.sdd

Can modify:
  /lib/features/history/history_screen.dart
  /lib/features/history/history_providers.dart
  /lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart
  /lib/features/history/route_group_providers.dart

Must:
  The History tab has a Liste/Karte switch; List is the default. The choice (`history_view`) and the map mode
    Lines or Heat (`history_map_mode`) are stored in preferences and come back after the app was closed
    and reopened or returned to from the background.
  The map view uses the History filters (activities, year, months, favourites, followed routes, search)
    through the same provider; changing a filter changes list and map alike. Sort and selection stay list-only.
  A long press on the map sets a pin; the my-location button also sets it to the current position (after the
    permission rules below). The pin can be dragged or removed, and a radius slider from `1` to `50` km
    (default `5`) draws the circle on the map. With a pin, only rides that match @AreaFilter remain.
  The area is part of the shared History filter: the list, the legend and the filter badge follow it; the badge
    counts it as one deviation and Reset clears it. It is not stored across app starts, like the other filters.
  While an area is set, rides without an outline are hidden until theirs is ready; setting an area starts
    the background fill at once.
  Only rides with a route are drawn. A ride without an outline gets one in the background, one at a time, and
    appears when it is ready.
  Lines mode draws one line per ride, thin and semi-transparent, in its activity type's colour, so a
    route ridden often looks denser. The nine types have nine distinct colours that stay readable on the light
    and the dark style; colour is never the only cue.
  The legend lists the types that occur, each with its icon and colour. Tapping a type shows or hides it
    by changing the shared activity filter.
  Heat mode draws the @HeatPoints of the visible rides as one heatmap layer in the app's primary colour;
    the filters and legend apply as in Lines mode.
  The camera starts framing all visible rides north-up. When the filters change it frames the new set once;
    a user gesture is never overridden afterwards.
  Tapping the map finds the rides under the tap with @OutlineHit. The nearest ride is highlighted and its
    preview card shows at the bottom: the cached preview, title, distance, duration, average speed and type,
    as on the History card, including the stored ascent or descent of #97 when the ride has one and nothing
    when it has none; the card is the History card, not a copy of it. Several hits can be swiped; the card shows `n/m`.
  A ride that is the best of its route group shows a best-time badge and, when its group has more rides,
    "n rides on this route"; a swipe through the group's rides shows each one's time. Rides outside a group
    have no badge.
  Tapping the card opens the ride detail as History does. Tapping empty map or the close control hides the card.
  The my-location button asks for location while the app is in use, never for Always and never for
    notifications. Granted: it shows the position and moves the camera there at zoom `15`, north-up.
    Denied: it shows a hint; denied for good: the hint offers the app settings. The position stream runs only
    while the map view is visible and the app is in the foreground.
  Without tiles (offline, style not loaded) the lines still show over a plain background, and the attribution
    stays visible.
  An empty history says so and offers no map or switch; a filter with no result says so over the map.
  A jump to a ride from Home shows the list, whichever view was stored.
  Location problems (not allowed, blocked, services off, no fix) show a hint instead of a position.
  The map follows the live map rules of the map spec for the style load, disposal and light/dark switch.
  Performance: outlines are read once into an in-memory cache by ride id and decoded on first use; a database
    emission changes only the rides that were added, changed or removed. The list query for the map selects
    only the outlines of rides that pass the filters.
  Map data is rebuilt off the UI thread and pushed only when the visible set changes: one GeoJSON source per
    type in Lines mode, one in Heat mode. Heat points are cached per ride, so a filter change only joins them.
    Filter changes and the radius slider are debounced to `150` ms; while the slider moves only the circle
    is redrawn.
  Tap hits reject by outline bounds first and never decode an outline whose bounds are far from the tap.
  The background fill handles one ride at a time, reads its trackpoints in one query, simplifies off the UI
    thread, writes in one transaction and yields between rides. It runs only while the map view is visible or
    an area is set, and stops when the app goes to the background.
  Deleting: a deleted ride (single, batch, or Discard after a ride) disappears from the lines, the heat, the
    legend counts, the list and the best-time badge with the next emission. A shown preview card whose ride is
    gone closes; a pin and radius stay. Its cached outline, heat points and preview are dropped. Deleting an
    original keeps its follows as ordinary rides with their outlines.
  No new network request is made; the map reads only data already on the device.

Must not:
  Read trackpoints for the overview, draw one map layer per ride, or show a live map inside a list item.
  Recompute a best time; it comes from @RouteGroup.
  Keep a second copy of the filters, or send the pin anywhere: it stays on the device.

Scenario: return to the app
  Given the map view was open
  When the app is closed and opened again
  Then the History tab shows the map view in the same mode

Scenario: tap on an overlapping stretch
  Given three rides pass the tapped point and two belong to one followed route
  When the map is tapped there
  Then the nearest ride is highlighted, the card shows `1/3`, and the best ride of its group has the badge

Scenario: rides around a place
  Given the map shows rides from two cities
  When a pin is set in one city with a radius of `10` km
  Then only the rides that come within `10` km of it remain, on the map and in the list, and the filter badge counts `1`

Scenario: deleting a ride shown on the map
  Given a ride's preview card is open on the map and the ride is part of a route group
  When the ride is deleted in History
  Then its line and heat points are gone, the card closes, the group's best time is recomputed without it,
    and no outline row, cached heat points or preview file of that ride remain

Scenario: deleting while the outline is being computed
  Given the background fill is computing the outline of a ride
  When the ride is deleted before the outline is written
  Then no outline row is created and nothing fails

Scenario: hiding a type
  Given the map shows longboard and ski rides
  When the ski type is turned off in the legend
  Then the ski lines disappear and the list shows only longboard rides too

Example:
  `history_view`: `list` by default, then `map`
  `history_map_mode`: `lines` by default, then `heat`

Tasks:
  [ ] #96 Performance and deletion: in-memory outline cache, isolate work, debounce, cascade and atomic batch delete, tests for both scenarios.
  [ ] #96 Schema version with `ride_outlines`: `7` once #97 (elevation, version `6`) is on `main`, else `6`; the upgrade steps stay in order.
  [ ] #96 `ride_outlines` upgrade step, outline at save, background fill for old rides.
  [ ] #96 Domain: @RideOutline, @OutlineHit, @HeatPoints, @AreaFilter (EXACT).
  [ ] #96 Overview map widget in `/lib/map` with lines, heat and position layers.
  [ ] #96 History switch, legend, preview card pager, pin and radius slider, preferences.
  [ ] #96 `CHANGELOG.md` and l10n (de, en); no privacy-policy change, there is no new data flow.

Done when:
  `flutter analyze` is clean, `flutter test` passes and `specdd lint` passes.
  The overview with many rides, the position button and the tap pager are checked on an Android and an iOS device.
